ss signals** \u2014 TODOs, commented-out code, ignored errors, or obviously untested risky logic in the diff.\n\nEvidence standard: This monitor assesses the change and its validation design; execution and merge eligibility are tracked by separate CI gates. Current-HEAD execution results may be pending or unavailable to this runner. Do not lower or cap the score, or add a rationale caveat, solely because current-HEAD test or CI execution evidence is unavailable. Base the score and rationale on concrete coverage, test quality, and correctness signals in the change. If execution results are available, distinguish observed passes or failures from source inspection and use only results attributable to the relevant revision. Report verified failures and substantive coverage gaps. Never claim tests passed or gates are clean from source inspection, and never present older-commit results as current-HEAD validation.\n\nScore from 0 to 100 (higher = more confidence):\n- 0-20: Critical correctness defects or no meaningful tests for risky behavior\n- 21-40: Minimal or shallow coverage\n- 41-60: Moderate coverage, gaps on critical parsing/provider/retrieval paths\n- 61-80: Good coverage, gates would catch most issues\n- 81-100: Thorough behavioral coverage (unit + integration/canary where relevant), appropriate validation design, and no substantive correctness concerns\n\nAfter your analysis, output ONLY this JSON object as the very last line of your response:\n\n{\"value\": <number 0-100>, \"rationale\": \"<1-2 sentence explanation>\"}"
